When working with utility types like Partial, I see that it makes fields optional, allowing for values like `T|undefined`, meaning an empty object is okay. But I realize there's an issue with the class declaration `class A<T> { value:T }` because T has no default value. The field needs an initializer, but if `value` were initialized or marked with `value!`, then the Partial assignment would be valid. I'm really going through the nuances here!"}]}
